    "created_at": "2019-04-03T16:01:02Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-04-03T16:01:02Z",
    "body": "I've always assumed they had constructors (and [[Construct]] methods), just throwing ones.\r\n\r\nI think it'd be very strange to have callable interface objects exist at all, and be reachable via the `.constructor` property, if they are not also [[Construct]]able.\r\n\r\nIn practice it doesn't matter much, but I do prefer keeping [[Construct]] and just saying that it throws for things without a constructor in the IDL.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
